Independent original Zero archive review, 2026-11-17

Reviewed tools/archive.zero and frozen native binaries. No implementation
changes were made by this reviewer. No unresolved correctness issue was found
within the documented bounds and no-concurrent-writers contract.

22 independent checks passed, supplementing the author's separate suite:
Windows PE under Wine packed, verified, listed and extracted nested paths,
repeated basenames, Unicode names, empty files, binary bytes and multi-chunk
content. Linux and Windows encoding of the same manifest/data was byte-identical.
Existing archives and destination trees were preserved. Damaged content and a
checksummed traversal path were rejected before creating a destination.
CONIN$, CONOUT$ with extension, COM superscript-one and LPT superscript-two
aliases were rejected. Unicode case-alias extraction failed cleanly and removed
its newly owned tree. Executable manifest flags survived Windows-to-Linux
packing/extraction: executable files had 0700, data files0600 under the test
umask. Windows extraction also preserved contents. A checksummed unsupported
flag2 was rejected before mkdir on both hosts. No extracted code was executed.

Review findings
Workspace regions fit the stated allocation. Counts/index sizes are checked
before record traversal. Each data offset must equal the previous exact end;
remaining-length checks precede data hashing. The entire index, all paths and
all content checksums are validated before extraction creates its root.
Every file is exclusively created; partial-write, flush and close failures
enter cleanup restricted to the newly created destination tree. Existing
roots are refused before setting the ownership flag. Directory/file prefix
conflicts and ASCII case aliases are checked before mutation. The indexed
format requires canonical contiguous payloads with no unexplained trailing
bytes. Reserved entry flags accept only0/1 before choosing output modes.

Limits remain64 MiB,4096 files,255-byte paths and32 components. The path
preflight folds ASCII case only. Non-ASCII names that alias on a target
filesystem can still be refused during exclusive extraction; this is not a
promise of complete Unicode filename portability. Source manifest paths use
the process working directory. Filesystem mutation assumes no concurrent
writers; extraction is not an atomic transaction or a permission-preserving
backup system. FNV checksums detect corruption, not hostile forgery.
Windows evidence is Wine execution, not a physical Windows installation.

